    "etymology": {
     "text": "From the root ط ف ل of طِفْل “child”, with the abstract pattern فُعُولَة (Wiktionary: childhood).",
     "src": "Wiktionary (kaikki.org)"
    },
    "funFacts": [
     "The pattern فُعُولَة makes abstract nouns of a state: طُفُولَة childhood, أُمُومَة motherhood, رُجُولَة manliness."
    ],
    "pitfalls": [
