     }
    ],
    "antonyms": [],
    "etymology": {
     "text": "From the root ل ع ب of لَعِبَ “to play”; Wiktionary: toy, plaything; game; doll; (figuratively) laughingstock. Plurals لُعَب, لُعُبَات, لُعْبَات.",
     "src": "Wiktionary (kaikki.org)"
    },
    "funFacts": [
     "مَلْعَب, “a place of playing”, is a stadium or a pitch; لَاعِب is a player — the same root."
    ],
    "pitfalls": [
     "لُعْبَة (luʿba) is the toy or the game; لَعْبَة (laʿba) is one round, one go — the vowel of the first letter matters.",
     "For games modern Arabic often uses the plural أَلْعَاب: أَلْعَابُ الْفِيدْيُو “video games”; لُعَب is mostly “toys”."
    ],
    "subtleties": [
     "A non-human plural: اللُّعَبُ جَمِيلَةٌ “the toys are nice” — the adjective is feminine singular."
    ]
   }
